{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939277-the-rite-of-luna\u2019s-eye-scrying","id":939277,"title":"The Rite of Luna\u2019s Eye (Scrying?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-28T19:16:57-07:00","id":939277,"title":"The Rite of Luna\u2019s Eye (Scrying?)","content":"My question is if this is considered a form of scrying, like Vampire's Auspex's Clairvoyance or Mage's Correspondence's Scrying and Demon's Firmament's Scrying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Level Three<br /> <br /> The War of Rage made the Garou many enemies among the Fera that claim most of Africa as territory, and werewolves travel those lands at their own peril. As well, Garou cannot keep vigil over every place on Earth to spot places where the Wyrm will strike. With this rite, however, nothing is beyond the gaze of those Silent Striders standing watch from Tullu Demtu (p. 72). System: The ritemaster\u2019s player must make a successful Perception + Rituals roll against a difficulty based on the distance the Garou wishes to see:<br /> <br /> Distance Difficulty<br /> Less than 500 miles 5<br /> 500-1,000 miles 6<br /> 1,001-2,000 miles 7<br /> 2,001-3,000 miles 8<br /> More than 3,000 miles 9<br /> <br /> The number of successes the ritemaster\u2019s player scores on this roll determines how much the Garou can focus on a particular place:<br /> <br /> Successes Effect<br /> 1 A view as wide as a satellite image of a single location.<br /> 2 A view of an area the size of a small forest, and the ritemaster can view several such areas before the vision passes.<br /> 3 A view of an area as small as an acre, and the ritemaster can maintain this watch for as long as she remains conscious.<br /> 4 A view as little as a few yards to each side, allowing the Garou to identify individual humans and animals.<br /> 5 The Garou can peer through solid objects, such that he can observe the interior of a house or scrutinize a cave deep under the earth </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:43:37-07:00","id":939292,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you could describe the rite as having a scrying effect, but this isn't D&amp;D. There aren't specific schools of magic or types of spells in werewolf. Why do you ask? Do have a fetish or something that protects you from scrying, but you are concerned that a Garou might be able to watch you using this rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T20:03:32-07:00","id":939301,"title":"","content":"Mage the Ascension 20th offers the power for a mage with Correspondence 4 to &quot;ban&quot; certain &quot;objectives&quot; from affecting a certain area; for example, if the area is warded against fire, someone who threw fireballs, or created fire through Fire Element at the threshold of the ward or inside, simply wouldn't be able to; a ward with the &quot;ban&quot; being scrying would prevent other mages from scrying within the limits of the ward, or from a vampire with Auspex from using Clairvoyance to see what's through; in this specific case a Garou tried to use the rite in question to observe the warded area, I was wondering if it'd fall under &quot;scrying&quot; for warding purposes or not.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T00:39:14-07:00","id":939392,"title":"","content":"It's based on spirit magic, so correspondence wouldn't be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T01:15:47-07:00","id":939398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939277-the-rite-of-luna\u2019s-eye-scrying?p=939392#post939392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's based on spirit magic, so correspondence wouldn't be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is.<br /> <br /> It's a question of paradigm versus rules versus crossover.<br /> <br /> My train of thought being like this: A Dreamspeaker would believe everything he does is done with spirit-aid, for that is his paradigm. According to Mage rules he would still need only the Correpsondence sphere for the effect. Likewise if the Dreamspeaker would like to spy, he would also just need correspondence. That said, the correspondence block would work against sphere magick, hedge magic scrying, but also certain powers of Disciplines like Auspex 7. So, why should it not block a garou rite? Because spirits are involved in the rite? That doesn't make a Dreamspeaker's scrying unblockable without spirit sphere magick, or any other Dreamspeaker magick effect.<br /> <br /> If an actual spirit was to travel into the warded area and peek, the blocking might not work, although peeking could be prohibited. But a rite doesn't for the most part require an actual spirit doing anything. Possibly some spirit entity somewhere uses some Charm akin to the Domain Sense power to gather the information and present them to the person performing the rite. Such an effort should be blocked with correspondence, just like it blocks hedge magic and vampire disciplines without requiring the mage having access to vitae or being able to manipulate vampires...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or another taught. The correspondence block can actually block the distance component in every effect, since distances are the main focus of correspondence. So, if it can ward an area from all external fire effects, without forces needed, it should be able to remove the distance part of the scrying, even if done be a spirit or rite, making the scrying pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-29-2016, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T02:44:22-07:00","id":939415,"title":"","content":"If it's of any help; the character who set the ward is indeed a Dreamspeaker, so if anything it makes things more likely to conform to his paradigm; another objective of the ward had been &quot;spirits&quot; too; and the Gauntlet rating at the area where the ward was set is 10. Thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:58:44-07:00","id":939599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939277-the-rite-of-luna\u2019s-eye-scrying?p=939398#post939398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is.<br /> <br /> It's a question of paradigm versus rules versus crossover.<br /> <br /> If an actual spirit was to travel into the warded area and peek, the blocking might not work, although peeking could be prohibited. But a rite doesn't for the most part require an actual spirit doing anything. Possibly some spirit entity somewhere uses some Charm akin to the Domain Sense power to gather the information and present them to the person performing the rite. Such an effort should be blocked with correspondence, just like it blocks hedge magic and vampire disciplines without requiring the mage having access to vitae or being able to manipulate vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite the description of a Rite, if it was as you described it to be that will result into everyone having the capability of using said rituals without being werebeasts, if we take a look at the book and inspect this paragraph, you can tell that the <b>spirits</b> are the ones who answer the Rite, and without the presence of spirits none of this will work. Rites are indeed spiritual. If they weren't, any mortal who's capable of being taught will be able to use them which isn't true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The special ties werewolves have with the spirit world allow rites to function. In the dawn of time, shapeshifters struck a great pact \u2014 the Pact \u2014 with the spirits of Gaia. In return for the shapeshifters\u2019 fealty and service, <b>the spirits would imbue the werebeasts\u2019 rites with supernatural power. For this reason, no one but a shapeshifter can perform rites and expect them to work.</b> The spirits will not answer the call if they are not bound by the Pact to do so. This relationship is unique to the Garou and certain other Fera, and it makes the performance of these rites their sacred right and privilege, and theirs alone.<br /> <br /> <b>Rites have both religious and magical connotations, and they serve both social and mystical purposes</b>. Most rites can be performed in either the Umbra or the physical world. </div> </div> </div>Rites are performed by the werebeasts but processed by the <b>spirits</b>, hence if you are making a new rite. The werebeast won't invent it by himself, but will have a spirit to help him do so and grant him the said knowledge (similar to gifts, in a way.). As previously mentioned by <b>Asmodai</b> they include spirit magic(k). Rites also differ from gifts, a gift is something you learn and know. A rite can't work by itself, it needs a correspondence ( a material ) that the spirit responds to, they aren't something you can master as a Gift as far as I am concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rites are considered to be a natural way of affecting the natural order. They\u2019re part of how things work. Werewolves believe that if a rite is performed properly, the effect will occur naturally, just as a scientist would follow cause and effect. If you drop a rock, it will fall; if you perform a rite as it was handed down to you by your ancestor\u2019s ancestors, then the desired effect will occur. However, some rites do require Gnosis. These rites are particularly powerful breaches of the natural order. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 07-29-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T00:40:46-07:00","id":941084,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing, that spirits answer rites or that they are limited to werebeast (with some notable exceptions).<br /> <br /> I just state two pints.<br /> <br /> 1. Most Rites don't need an actual spirit present. Meaning, that garou can enact a Rite, even if on the same scene there is currently no spirit (awaken or slumbering) in the penumbra or the material world. Unless the Rite's description explicitly states, that a spirit is required (i.e. Rite of Binding) or carries out the Rites effect (i.e. Rite of the Sparrow) there are no actual spirits involved in the Rites effect. Sure, the spirits imbue the werebeast's Rites with power, but is that really a mechanical part of the Rite others can influence?<br /> If it is, you need to think about aspects like whether the imbueing of the Rite by the spiris can be blocked by means of magic(k). Or if the spirits can even witness the Garou performing the Rite in the first place.<br /> I wouldn't open that can of worms. I'd just assume a garou can perform a Rite at any time any where, if all the Rites specific prerequisites are met. If not the difficulty increases as per Bone Gnawer revised TB (or it is impossible).<br /> I would not normally argue, that the spirits can't imbue a garou's Rite at a specific location because they are warded off.<br /> <br /> 2. I argue, that while light and sound are technically part of the Forces sphere in Mage, the perceiving of anther location is solely a Correspondence effect. Warding an area of such an effect is also solely Correspondence. It doesn't make a mechanical difference if the effect was created by a Hermetic, Verbena or Dreamspeaker, although each has a very different idea of how such an effect comes to pass. Any Correspondence ward would ward any Correspondence effect. &quot;The Rite of Luna\u2019s Eye&quot; as described above is a akin to a Correspondence effect, and therefore would be blocked. I don't see that the Rite necessarily has a Spirit component (within the MtA rules). In any case, it wouldn't matter for a solely Correspondence ward would not only ward against solely Correspondence scrying, but also against Correspondence/(Life or Matter) Teleport or Correspndence/Forces long range fireballs and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}